* divide error! */
size_t size2alloc = 100, actual_alloced;
void *p;
pr_info("kmalloc( n) : Actual : Wastage : Waste %%\n");
while (1) {
p = kmalloc(size2alloc, GFP_KERNEL);
Note that the ksize() API works only on allocated slab memory; you cannot use it on the
return value from any of the page allocator APIs (which we saw in the Learning how to use
